# Cache headers (BUILD-PLAN.md §8, WP7): short TTL on HTML so content updates show up quickly,
# long + immutable on fingerprinted build assets (filenames are content-hashed by Vite, so a
# changed file always gets a new URL — safe to cache forever). Cloudflare *merges* same-named
# headers from every matching block rather than letting a later, more specific block override an
# earlier one — confirmed against a live deploy, where /_astro/* came back with both Cache-Control
# values concatenated into one invalid header. `! Cache-Control` explicitly unsets the broader
# rule's value first so the specific rule's value is the only one that ships.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
